# BookHunt × Lienzo — environment variables (Phase 1: ALL optional)
#
# Phase 1 runs with ZERO secrets: with none of these set, the app uses the
# built-in mock data layer (mock Google Books catalog, mock eBay results,
# mock Supabase-shaped listings/profiles, mock demo user).
# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in values only when wiring real services.
# Never commit a real .env — it is gitignored.

# --- Google Books API -------------------------------------------------------
# Corrected spelling (preferred):
VITE_GOOGLE_BOOKS_KEY=
# Legacy MISSPELLED spelling from the original code ("GOOLE"). Still honored
# as a fallback so an old .env keeps working — do not use for new setups:
VITE_GOOLE_BOOKS_KEY=

# --- BookHunt backend (bookhunt-back, Express/eBay) -------------------------
VITE_BACKEND_URL=
VITE_LOCAL_BACKEND_URL=

# --- Supabase (Phase E1 — wired) ---------------------------------------------
# When BOTH are set, the app uses the real Supabase backend (Auth + Postgres
# via @supabase/supabase-js); when either is absent it falls back to the
# built-in mock layer. Use the project's URL and its anon / publishable key —
# that key is a public client identifier; protect data with Row Level
# Security. The service_role / secret key is a REAL secret: server-side
# only, never expose it to the browser and never give it a VITE_ prefix.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# --- Cloudflare Turnstile (U28 — Supabase CAPTCHA protection) ---------------
# PUBLIC site key for the Turnstile widget. When set, the app renders the
# widget on the auth screens and sends a token with sign-up, sign-in and
# password-reset calls, which Supabase verifies server-side once CAPTCHA
# protection is enabled in the Supabase dashboard (Authentication →
# Settings → CAPTCHA protection, provider: Turnstile). When empty, no
# widget renders and auth calls go without a token (pre-U28 behavior).
# ORDER MATTERS: set this in Vercel (Production + Preview) and deploy
# BEFORE enabling the dashboard toggle — once protection is on, Supabase
# rejects tokenless auth calls. The matching SECRET key goes ONLY in the
# Supabase dashboard; never in the front end, never with a VITE_ prefix.
VITE_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY=

# --- Firebase (LEGACY — no longer used by the app) ---------------------------
# Kept here only to document what the original .env contained. The Phase 1
# code has no Firebase imports; these values are ignored.
VITE_FIREBASE_APIKEY=
VITE_FIREBASE_AUTHDOMAIN=
VITE_FIREBASE_PROJECTID=
VITE_FIREBASE_STORAGEBUCKET=
VITE_FIREBASE_MESSAGINGSENDERID=
VITE_FIREBASE_APPID=
VITE_FIREBASE_MEASUREMENTID=
